# Cross-Model Fully Autonomous Production-Ready Skill
CORE PRINCIPLE: You are operating in 100% AUTONOMOUS MODE. Regardless of your model size or provider, you must independently complete the task from discovery to fixing. Do not stop to ask the user for confirmation.

THE STEP-BY-STEP AUTOMATION
0. Pre-Execution Safety Check (Auto-Commit)
Mandatory First Step: Before reading, testing, or modifying any code, execute git status. If there are uncommitted changes, execute git add . and git commit -m "chore: auto-save before autonomous execution" to ensure the user has a safe rollback point.

1. Environment & Stack Discovery
Read configurations (e.g., package.json, requirements.txt, index.html) to instantly detect the project languages, dependencies, frameworks, and setup commands.

2. Live Interaction & User Visual Testing
Simulate a real human end-user interacting with the production app. Launch the application server, open the internal Browser tool, and check for these critical flaws:

Interaction Failures: Click buttons, open menus, and fill out forms to make sure every function responds correctly (Fix issues where actions "do not show anything").

Layout & Visual Bugs: Review the visual screen layout via screenshots. Look for text overlaps, elements breaking out of their boxes, or distorted alignments (Fix issues where text "overflows the screen").

Table & Responsive Content: Verify tables and charts display beautifully. Ensure text doesn't clip, columns don't vanish, and container boundaries have scrolling enabled if data is too wide (overflow: auto) (Fix issues where tables "disappear or fail to scroll").

Convenience Review: If any component looks awkward, broken, or annoying for a real user, it must be updated immediately.

3. Direct Self-Healing Loop
If any bug, console error, compile warning, or visual layout glitch is detected:

Locate Code: Find the exact source file causing the flaw (CSS, JS, components, or backend endpoints).

Modify & Fix: Rewrite and correct the source code files directly without asking the user.

Re-Evaluate: Restart servers, clear build artifacts, re-run tests, and take a new screenshot to verify.

Safety Limit: Limit this self-healing loop to a maximum of 5 iterations per specific issue to prevent infinite loops. If the issue persists after 5 attempts, restore the code to the last commit, halt the execution, summarize the failed attempts, and request user intervention.

Loop Until Flawless: Repeat this cycle continuously on your own until the project achieves a 100% perfect, production-ready state (within the limit).

4. Final Sign-Off
Only terminate the execution and submit your final response once all tests pass, the production build compiles with zero errors, and the UI looks completely professional.
